{
  "notes": "Per-band rank choices (owner ruling 3, sim-accuracy round 9). Below level 60 the site rewrites a rotation's ranked spells: by default each casts the highest rank learned that is not above the rank the curated rotation names, so a deliberate lower rank there is kept. A row here overrides that for one spec's authored spell id from from_level through to_level: the rotation casts that rank instead, higher or lower. A row may name a preset (bare or raid) and then applies only to a request simmed under it; one with none applies to both. Level 60 runs the curated rotation as written, which carries the raid choice; a row at 60 names its preset. A row is adopted where the fight is mana-bound and the rank raises the band's published number beyond the error at seeds 1 and 50001, 10000 iterations; a healer row never turns a fight that runs dry into one that ends with mana unspent, and every healer row below 60 is measured on its own band's heal profile (data/curated/heal-profile.json bands). A mana gate is not evidence on its own (owner ruling 2, round 10): a row behind a gated line also wins with the gate taken away, where the spec then runs dry. The evidence is in design/reviews/2026-11-02-sim-audit-round9/ranks.md and the round-10 ranks.md and healprofile.md beside it. Defensive cooldowns (Divine Protection, Divine Shield, Ice Barrier and the like) are never rank choices. sim/request embeds a copy (make rank-choices-sync); TestEmbeddedRankChoicesMatchCurated holds it to this file.",
